# OPERATOR STATE. `make pi-ship` does not overwrite the copy on the Pi
# (PI_OWNED in the Makefile). git holds only the seed for a fresh
# install. Edit it in `sudo pf tui`, Agent > Filtering > "DNS record
# types", or by hand on the Pi, then `sudo pf apply`.
#
# The resolver of the agent segment answers only A queries. The Pi gives
# an empty answer to all other types (TXT, MX, SRV, NULL, ANY, CAA, NS,
# SOA, a public PTR, ...), and never forwards them. An A answer gets to
# the agent as a maximum of 16 addresses, under the name that the agent
# asked for, with no CNAMEs. An LLM over DNS answers with TXT, and a
# CNAME target is also text.
#
# A line here forwards a name and type pair as before:
#   <name> <TYPE> [<TYPE>...]    exactly that name
#   *.<name> <TYPE> [<TYPE>...]  every name under it, not <name> itself
# A type is spelled as dns.jsonl spells it: TXT, MX, SRV, NS, SOA, PTR,
# CNAME, or TYPE<n> for any other (NULL is TYPE10, ANY TYPE255, CAA
# TYPE257). AAAA, HTTPS and SVCB are filtered before this list, on all
# segments. An entry for one of these types changes nothing, and pf dns
# writes a warning for it.
#
# A line that does not parse is skipped (journalctl -u
# pi-fortress-dns-agent-go shows which), and its pairs stay filtered.
# Empty means no overrides. This is the default.
